# NOTE: Assertions have been autogenerated by utils/update_mir_test_checks.py UTC_ARGS: --version 6
# RUN: llc -mtriple=amdgpu9.0a-amd-amdhsa -amdgpu-s-branch-bits=5 -start-before=amdgpu-pre-ra-long-branch-reg -stop-after=branch-relaxation -verify-machineinstrs -o - %s | FileCheck %s

# In a callable function, the SGPR pair that the long branch expansion
# (S_GETPC_B64/S_ADD_U32/S_ADDC_U32/S_SETPC_B64) writes must not be a
# callee-saved register or the return address, unless it is saved and
# restored. Nothing saves the reserved pair: amdgpu-pre-ra-long-branch-reg
# reserves it before RA, the prolog-epilog shift-down may move it after RA, and
# branch relaxation writes it without scavenging.
#
# With -amdgpu-s-branch-bits=5, the 4 x 4 v_nop_e64 in each arm are out of
# range for a direct branch. The pre-RA estimate counts each INLINEASM as one
# 8-byte instruction and only looks at blocks that end in an unconditional
# branch, hence several small INLINEASM per arm instead of one big one.
#
# The machineFunctionInfo is what ISel sets up for a callable wave64 function.
# sgprForEXECCopy keeps s[100:101] reserved until si-lower-sgpr-spills, as in
# the real pipeline.
#
# On gfx90a, the callee-saved SGPRs are s30-s39, s48-s55, s64-s71, s80-s87 and
# s96-s105; s[30:31] holds the return address.

# High SGPR pressure: the inline asm clobbers every non-callee-saved SGPR pair
# (s0-s29, s40-s47, s56-s63, s72-s79, s88-s95) plus most callee-saved ones.
# No pair is both free and safe before RA, so none may be reserved: the long
# branch must use a register found by the scavenger (s[4:5], dead after the
# clobber). Without the fix it uses s[100:101], which is callee-saved but not
# saved in the prologue.

--- |
  define void @high_sgpr_pressure() #0 {
    ret void
  }

  define void @low_sgpr_pressure() #0 {
    ret void
  }

  ; nounwind avoids most CFI_INSTRUCTIONs in the output.
  attributes #0 = { nounwind }
...
---
name:            high_sgpr_pressure
tracksRegLiveness: true
machineFunctionInfo:
  scratchRSrcReg:  '$sgpr0_sgpr1_sgpr2_sgpr3'
  frameOffsetReg:  '$sgpr33'
  stackPtrOffsetReg: '$sgpr32'
  sgprForEXECCopy: '$sgpr100_sgpr101'
body:             |
  ; CHECK-LABEL: name: high_sgpr_pressure
  ; CHECK: bb.0:
  ; CHECK-NEXT:   successors: %bb.1(0x40000000), %bb.6(0x40000000)
  ; CHECK-NEXT:   liveins: $sgpr16, $sgpr34, $sgpr35, $sgpr36, $sgpr37, $sgpr38, $sgpr39, $sgpr48, $sgpr49, $sgpr50, $sgpr51, $sgpr52, $sgpr53, $sgpr54, $sgpr55, $sgpr64, $sgpr65, $sgpr66, $sgpr67, $sgpr68, $sgpr69, $sgpr70, $sgpr71, $sgpr80, $sgpr81, $sgpr82, $sgpr83, $sgpr84, $sgpr85, $sgpr86, $sgpr87, $sgpr96, $sgpr97, $sgpr30_sgpr31
